From: Actions-OpenWrt <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] tcp: bbr: retain BBRv3 module version metadata

Lean enables CONFIG_MODULE_STRIPPED, which intentionally turns
MODULE_VERSION() into a disabled MODULE_INFO_STRIP() declaration. BBRv3's
generation must remain observable at build time and through the module sysfs
version attribute, so emit this one identity field directly. Other module
metadata remains stripped.

---
 net/ipv4/tcp_bbr.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr.c b/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr.c
--- a/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/tcp_bbr.c
@@ -2404,4 +2404,4 @@ MODULE_AUTHOR("David Morley <morleyd@google.com>");
 
 MODULE_LICENSE("Dual BSD/GPL");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("TCP BBR (Bottleneck Bandwidth and RTT)");
-MODULE_VERSION(__stringify(BBR_VERSION));
+MODULE_INFO(version, __stringify(BBR_VERSION));
